{"id":1191,"date":"2021-02-25T15:45:08","date_gmt":"2021-02-25T15:45:08","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/?post_type=rdrcnews&#038;p=1191"},"modified":"2021-02-25T21:08:11","modified_gmt":"2021-02-25T21:08:11","slug":"rdrcre-cap-the-mayor-visits-the-rockaway-re-development-project","status":"publish","type":"rdrcnews","link":"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/rdrcnews\/rdrcre-cap-the-mayor-visits-the-rockaway-re-development-project\/","title":{"rendered":"RDRCRe-Cap The Mayor Visits The Rockaway B21st Street Re-Development Project"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><span style=\"color: #b87614;\">The B21st Street Re-Development Project<\/span><!--more--><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">On Monday, February 22nd, RDRC welcomed <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/www1.nyc.gov\/office-of-the-mayor\/\">Mayor Bill De Blasio<\/a><\/span> to the <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/rockawaydevrevcorp\/photos\/p.878211583027422\/878211583027422\/\">Far Rockaway Beach 21st Street Re-Development Project<\/a><\/span>. &#8220;Topping Off&#8221; Ceremony. In addition to Mayor de Blasio, RDRC President &amp; CEO Kevin Alexander joined by <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/www.queensbp.org\/contact\/\">Queens Borough President Donovan Richards<\/a><\/span>, <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/www.nysenate.gov\/senators\/james-sanders-jr\">NYS State Senator James Sanders, Jr.<\/a><\/span>, <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/nyassembly.gov\/mem\/Khaleel-M-Anderson\">NYS Assemblyman Khaleel Anderson<\/a><\/span>, <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/www.tcbinc.org\/\">Jesse Batus, Senior Project Manager, The Community Builders<\/a><\/span>, <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/edc.nyc\/\">NY Economic Development Corporation President James Padgett<\/a><\/span>, <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/www1.nyc.gov\/site\/hpd\/index.page\">HPD Housing Preservation &amp; Development Commissioner Louise Campbell<\/a><\/span>, and <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/www1.nyc.gov\/site\/ddc\/index.page\">Department of Design &amp; Construction<\/a><\/span> Commissioner Lorraine Grillo. The following is an excerpt of the remarks made by Alexander.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">&#8220;The Beach 21st Street Project is an excellent example of that commitment to change that includes our partnership with the City and leaders such as Rockaways own, <\/span><br \/>\n<span style=\"color: #000080;\">then-City Councilman and now Queens Borough President Donovan Richards, at the community level with our <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/www1.nyc.gov\/site\/queenscb14\/index.page\">Community Board 14<\/a><\/span>, and a coalition of community and faith-based organizations known as the <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/edc.nyc\/project\/downtown-far-rockaway\">DFR Working Group<\/a><\/span>. <\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">Ultimately, the collaboration ends where it all begins, with our residents who deservedly will have the opportunity for generations to come, to benefit from the manifestation of the DFR Redevelopment Project that is so much more than an affordable housing project \u2013 jobs, careers, new commercial space for local businesses and entrepreneurs, community space for new and existing CBO&#8217;s to expand, open spaces to host community events and activities, a world-class library, and beautiful streetscapes supported by weather-resistant and upgraded infrastructure.&#8221;<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">The CBO&#8217;s website is the primary source of news in the Downtown Far Rockaway neighborhood. It provides information on community happenings, business opportunities, invitations, and information on our programs and services. Join our\u00a0<span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a class=\"editor-rtfLink\" style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/visitor.r20.constantcontact.com\/manage\/optin?v=001f-KEXzn5tO1N9oJq961YEq-GzWV1xAIboWtxqYSZXpq5yO1UUgfaSniqtf1xswR-A8b9vOUVS7HXpQIU0guJvspmnPOyroO7_bzKHe449Dw%3D\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">weekly electronic newsletter<\/a><\/span> for upcoming happenings and business resources; subscribers will also receive periodic invites to special RDRC events. To have your campaigns highlighted in our weekly newsletter, please provide all graphic work in JPEG, PNG, PDF formats (hi-rez) along with detailed content. For more information about the weekly newsletter, email Valerie N. Stevens to communityrelations@rdrc.org, or call 718.327.5300 ext. 316.<\/span><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>The B21st Street Re-Development Project<\/p>\n","protected":false},"featured_media":1192,"parent":0,"menu_order":0,"template":"","meta":{"_acf_changed":false},"class_list":["post-1191","rdrcnews","type-rdrcnews","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/rdrcnews\/1191","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/rdrcnews"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/rdrcnews"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1192"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1191"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}